{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794746765,"nonce":"yDwnoeqy7PyNE6crX2mSaXCZF2U=","message":"Built in ~/Vibranium/hxn-gpu-gles (local commit a892911, not yet on GitHub). EGL and OpenGL ES load at run time through khronos-egl and glow, so one build runs on Mesa, Android's system EGL, and ANGLE through HXN_GPU_GLES_EGL. Bindings (sources/) numbers uniform-block binding points and texture units from GLSL_BINDINGS and assigns them by name. Context.completed() waits on an EGL 1.5 fence from a blocking thread when the display has EGL_KHR_fence_sync, else calls glFinish. The check (render read back after completed, a textured pass, a mapped buffer read) passes on Ash, hxcpp and CPPIA on macOS through ANGLE (Electron's, over Metal; no fence sync), and on stock HashLink on the NUC with Mesa on the Intel GPU (fence path). examples/present draws to an X11 window with createWindowContext(window, visual); not run yet (the NUC has no Xvfb), CI runs it under Xvfb. CI is written for Linux (Mesa llvmpipe), and macOS and Windows with the runner's Chrome's ANGLE.","files":null}]}